WorldWind Kotlin 2.1.1 Android label and contour-render review

Original source: earth.worldwind:worldwind-android:2.1.1, published by the
WorldWind Kotlin project, https://github.com/WorldWindEarth/WorldWindKotlin .
The original publication POM identifies Eugene Maksymenko as developer and
declares Apache License, Version 2.0. The complete original source archive,
an upstream copy of LICENSE is retained here. The reproducible build retains
the checksum-verified original POM, module metadata, AAR and source archive
under its isolated .openai build directory. Generated build-manifest.json
records the source URLs, original hashes, local source fingerprint and patch.

Local changes, 2026-11-05, for isolated Shantu Android research review:
- MvtLabelCollider.kt: Android physical text bounds, real text anchor,
  terrain-consistent projection and independent per-repeat line collision.
- MvtCurvedLineLabel.kt: shared prepare/draw snapshot, displayed-terrain
  projection, perspective-correct segment mapping and per-repeat validity.
- AndroidMvtLabelMetrics.kt and MvtLabelCollisionMath.kt: new measurement and
  bounds helpers, provided under Apache License, Version 2.0. The visible
  repeat iterator in MvtLabelCollisionMath is adapted from the above
  WorldWind 2.1.1 MvtCurvedTextPlacer arc-length algorithm; it retains its
  middle-waypoint phase, repeat spacing and GlyphRun representation, while
  skipping offscreen repeat indices and using Double arc-length arithmetic.
- The metrics LRU is capped at 4096 entries; texts over 256 UTF-16 units are
  measured but not cached. Text content and road geometry are not changed.
- Upside-down, excessively curved or inaccurately projected name repeats are
  omitted independently; other valid repeats of the same feature remain.

Local change, 2026-11-06:
- MvtBatchedLineTile.kt: added a default-null per-range render-time color
  transform. It runs after unpacking the cached range color into the current
  draw state's color and before DrawShapeState captures that color for its
  primitive. It does not rebuild geometry or retain source coordinates.
- MvtBatchedLineTileColorHookCheck.kt exercises the same range-to-draw-state
  color method, including dark-to-white and bright-to-black output and alpha
  preservation. The Android app supplies a stateless WCAG contrast callback
  only while elevation fill and contours are both enabled.

No Ovital source code or binary implementation is included in this patch.
This patch alone is not an installed or visually validated APK.
